# Citation File Format (CFF) -- https://citation-file-format.github.io/
#
# This file lets GitHub render a "Cite this repository" button and lets
# Zenodo, OSF, ContentMine and most citation managers (Zotero, BibDesk,
# Mendeley) ingest a structured citation in BibTeX, RIS, CSL-JSON or
# EndNote with a single click.
#
# Whenever a new release of the Gold Standard is tagged, update both
# `version` and `date-released` below, and regenerate the DOI via the
# Zenodo / GitHub integration.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use the Gold Standard GBFS France dataset in your research,
  please cite both this software/data record and the companion paper
  (see preferred-citation below).
type: dataset
title: "Gold Standard GBFS France: an audited national reference dataset for bike-sharing systems"
abstract: >-
  The Gold Standard GBFS France is an audited, certified and openly
  released national reference dataset built from the systematic audit
  of the 122 French GBFS systems published on
  transport.data.gouv.fr and MobilityData. It contains 46,307
  certified stations covering 57 urban areas, classified by a taxonomy
  of five anomaly classes (A1-A5) and enriched by spatial joining with
  INSEE Filosofi, BAAC (Cerema), BD TOPO, OpenStreetMap and the FUB
  Cycling Barometer. The dataset is distributed as a versioned Parquet
  file together with an audit report, a JSON Schema, a Frictionless
  Data Package descriptor and a Croissant JSON-LD manifest.

